--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DESIGN (no parity shortcut; DRY/ADR-006 — page reuses the A3 feature view)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web unit `AutomationActivityFeed.tsx` is an UNROUTED, purely presentational sub-surface: it receives
`history`, `historyStats`, `isLoading`, `liveEvents`, `connectionState` as props from the Automations page
and calls no API hook of its own (only `useTranslation`). The parity-manifest record therefore declares
NO API data sources — "renders from navigation args / local state".

A complete A3 parity port of the SAME web file already exists as the shared feature view
io.teslasync.android.featureviews.automationactivityfeed (com/teslasync/feature-views/AutomationActivityFeed).
It owns the single GlassPanel, the always-on header (Activity glyph + "Recent Activity" + the Live/Reconnecting
connection chip + the run-summary stats), the live SSE event rows, and every history data state
(loading / content / empty / + host-feed error+retry). This A7 page is therefore a thin host (the
GasPriceAutoPollPage precedent): it binds the page's LOCAL snapshot and renders that one shared surface
verbatim — never re-implementing the panel/states/strings (anti-duplication, ADR-006).

Data : no API source (manifest). AutomationActivityFeedSource (local-state seam) -> AutomationActivityFeedViewModel
       hoists the snapshot into state: StateFlow<UiState<AutomationActivityData>> + liveEvents + connectionState
       (P1/S8 shape). With no automations feed wired into the Android DataContainer (and DataContainer is
       outside this artifact's allowed files), the production source yields a connected, empty snapshot — the
       honest local state for an unrouted surface handed no execution history — which the feature view renders
       as the friendly empty surface with the "Live" indicator, exactly as the web component renders with empty
       props. The loading and content surfaces are first-class, reachable phases of the same StateFlow (init =
       UiState.loading(); a non-empty history projects to UiPhase.Content). No HTTP touches the view.
SI    : no unit-bearing field (counts, a 0-100 percent, the millisecond durations the backend already computed);
       the feature view formats at the render boundary (S5). No SI conversion at this layer.

